@startuml sequence_diagram_google_login
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - AA02 Successful Google Sign-In (OIDC Authorization Code Flow + PKCE)

actor User as "Client / User"
participant SPA as "SPA (Front-End)\nGoogleSignInButton /\nGoogleCallbackPage"
participant Routes as "AuthRoutes"
participant Validator as "ValidationMiddleware\n(Joi)"
participant Controller as "AuthController"
participant ExtService as "ExternalAuthenticationService"
participant Store as "IAuthorizationStateStore\n(InMemory)"
participant IdP as "IExternalIdentityProvider\n(GoogleOidcProvider)"
participant Google as "Google Identity Services\n(OIDC Provider)"
participant Repo as "IUserRepository"
database DB as "Database\n(Persistence)"
participant Service as "UserService"
participant JWT as "ITokenService\n(JWT)"
participant Mapper as "UserResponseMapper"

note over User, Mapper
    Success path only: linked, active account with at least one role.
    Account-resolution outcomes (new account, inactive, no role, e-mail conflict): SD 2.
    Cancellation, invalid payload and authentication failures: SD 3.
end note

== 1. Start external authentication ==

User -> SPA : clicks "Continue with Google"\n(login page, next to local login - AA01)
activate SPA
SPA -> Routes : POST /api/v1/auth/google/authorization
activate Routes
note right of Routes : public rate limiter +\nCache-Control: no-store
Routes -> Controller : startGoogleLogin(req, res)
activate Controller
Controller -> ExtService : startAuthorization()
activate ExtService
ExtService -> IdP : createAuthorizationRequest()
activate IdP
IdP -> IdP : generate state, nonce, codeVerifier\ncodeChallenge = S256(codeVerifier)
IdP --> ExtService : { authorizationUrl, state, nonce, codeVerifier }
deactivate IdP
ExtService -> Store : save(state, { provider: GOOGLE, nonce,\ncodeVerifier, expiresAt: now + 10 min })
activate Store
Store --> ExtService : stored
deactivate Store
ExtService --> Controller : ExternalAuthorizationDTO { authorizationUrl, state }
deactivate ExtService
Controller --> SPA : 200 OK { authorizationUrl, state }
deactivate Controller
deactivate Routes

SPA -> SPA : sessionStorage.set("oidc_state", state)
SPA -> Google : browser redirect to authorizationUrl\n(response_type=code, client_id, redirect_uri,\nscope="openid email profile", state, nonce,\ncode_challenge, code_challenge_method=S256)
deactivate SPA
activate Google

== 2. Authentication at Google (outside LaPrizza) ==

Google -> User : Google sign-in and consent screen
User -> Google : Google credentials + consent
note over User, Google
    The Google password is entered only on Google's pages.
    LaPrizza never receives, collects or stores it (AC 5).
end note
Google --> SPA : 302 redirect_uri\n/auth/callback/google?code=...&state=...
deactivate Google
activate SPA

== 3. Complete authentication in LaPrizza ==

SPA -> SPA : query state equals sessionStorage "oidc_state"\nremove stored state
SPA -> Routes : POST /api/v1/auth/google/callback\n{ code, state }
activate Routes
Routes -> Validator : ValidationMiddleware.validate(schemas.googleCallback)\n(req, res, next)
activate Validator
Validator --> Routes : next()  (payload valid)
deactivate Validator

Routes -> Controller : completeGoogleLogin(req, res)
activate Controller
Controller -> ExtService : completeAuthorization(new ExternalCallbackDTO(req.body))
activate ExtService

ExtService -> ExtService : verifyIdentity(code, state)
activate ExtService
ExtService -> Store : consume(state)
activate Store
Store --> ExtService : pending { provider, nonce, codeVerifier }\n(entry removed: single use)
deactivate Store

ExtService -> IdP : exchangeAndVerify(code, codeVerifier, nonce)
activate IdP
IdP -> Google : POST token endpoint\n(code, client_id, client_secret,\nredirect_uri, code_verifier)
activate Google
Google --> IdP : { id_token, access_token, expires_in }
deactivate Google
IdP -> IdP : verify id_token: signature (Google JWKS),\niss, aud = client_id, exp, nonce;\nemail_verified = true; discard access_token
IdP --> ExtService : ExternalIdentityClaims\n{ provider: GOOGLE, subject, email, emailVerified, name }
deactivate IdP
deactivate ExtService

ExtService -> ExtService : resolveAccount(claims)
activate ExtService
ExtService -> Repo : findByExternalIdentity(GOOGLE, subject)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB : SELECT users + user_external_identities\nWHERE provider = 'GOOGLE' AND subject = $1
activate DB
DB --> Repo : user row + identity rows
deactivate DB
Repo --> ExtService : user (linked; current internal roles)
deactivate Repo
deactivate ExtService

ExtService -> ExtService : assertCanStartSession(user):\nuser.isActive() and user.hasActiveRole()

ExtService -> Service : issueAuthToken(user)
activate Service
Service -> JWT : generateToken({ sub: user.getId().getValue(),\nemail: user.getEmail().getValue(), roles: user.getRoles() })
activate JWT
JWT --> Service : accessToken (string)
deactivate JWT
Service -> Mapper : toDTO(user)
activate Mapper
Mapper --> Service : UserResponseDTO
deactivate Mapper
Service --> ExtService : AuthTokenDTO { accessToken, tokenType: "Bearer",\nexpiresIn: tokenService.expiresIn, user }
deactivate Service

ExtService --> Controller : AuthTokenDTO
deactivate ExtService
Controller --> SPA : 200 OK { accessToken, tokenType: "Bearer",\nexpiresIn, user { id, name, email, roles, active, ... } }
deactivate Controller
deactivate Routes

SPA -> SPA : keep the token as defined by AA04;\nroles taken only from the back-end response (AA03)
SPA --> User : navigate to the start page allowed\nby the internal roles (WEB03)
deactivate SPA

@enduml